{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: preserve the independent review's out-of-scope performance-runner finding as a bounded child of #22297. This does not reopen or broaden the approved batch-test head. Queue it behind the active main-CI repair and pending approved landings; take it in a suitable short work interval without dropping full Tail I7. Confirm current bases and availability at actual start.\n\nThe [worker subprocess boundary](cmd/gitseq-perf/main.go@0afa98aa26be6756682f28defb081043ecc8efa2:533) feeds CombinedOutput into its JSON decoder. [The worker](cmd/gitseq-perf/main.go@0afa98aa26be6756682f28defb081043ecc8efa2:248) emits its result to stdout, while the [scenario](internal/perfscenario/run.go@0afa98aa26be6756682f28defb081043ecc8efa2:156) explicitly invokes runtime.GC. I independently reproduced the failure under Go1.26.7 at exact 0afa98aa26be6756682f28defb081043ecc8efa2, using a disposable depth-10 cold_status fixture and a temporary test overlay: the ordinary worker succeeds, but the same successful worker with GODEBUG=gctrace=1 fails at the parent decoder with invalid character 'g'. Its GC diagnostics precede a valid JSON result in the combined stream. The child process itself returned success. The attached probe and output are diagnostic evidence, not a performance comparison, retained benchmark, or claim that ordinary default runs fail. Both cited source blobs match their live d70d8fe6 artifact bases despite inherited ordinary staleness.\n\nSeparate stdout from stderr at this structured worker-result boundary. Decode and validate stdout only; preserve useful stderr on process and decoding failures, and retain nonzero exit, timeout, unknown-field and result-validation behavior. Keep any successful diagnostic handling simple and explicit. Do not solve this by suppressing runtime diagnostics, weakening JSON validation, changing the sample schema, increasing timing budgets, or replacing every CombinedOutput in unrelated build/benchstat helpers.\n\nIn a fresh request/perf-worker-stdout worktree, add a deterministic successful-worker stderr regression and relevant failing-worker/invalid-JSON controls. The attached real GC-diagnostic probe supplies an integration reproduction; tests must show the old mixed-stream behavior fails and the repaired boundary accepts the successful result without treating diagnostics as JSON. Run focused package checks and appropriate build/vet gates with accurately attributed toolchain evidence. No full envelope, loaded-machine run or broad benchmark campaign is needed for this stream separation. Publish the exact-path artifact, obtain independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratify the verdict, land through the sealed merge path, push source/sequence/receipt refs, verify green main CI and clean up only the owned worktree and branch. No running-service change is requested.","body":{"branch":"request/perf-worker-stdout","conditions":"Decode performance-worker results from stdout alone while retaining separate diagnostics and real process failures; deterministic stderr and failure controls, unchanged validation and performance contract, independent exact-head review, sealed landing, pushed refs, green CI and owned cleanup.","head":"0afa98aa26be6756682f28defb081043ecc8efa2","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:05db19d0a0c499134d89982cb0b106d868d9cc9a, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6b52728d756db98c66efcc1ded1ed67ac1d64bf6, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9f697435b24f23f367e53a7ce87d8a54daf0cd47, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e00b75c9873251b2a529dab6e8cc974a7fb6fdd2 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c819676fead7d19fdd20633b48dc16c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015bb3acec403ed0d43bcd2a3c38bd188f7740ef, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478